# records/ — what freezes here, and what never does

At each release, `ultra records freeze <version>` renders that cut's evidence
into `records/<version>/`:

- `trace.md` / `trace.json` — the derived traceability matrix (WP.21), as
  rendered at the freeze;
- `test.json` / `e2e.json` — COPIES of the recorded runs (`.ultra/` is
  gitignored exhaust; the freeze is what makes a run durable), with their
  real mtimes and the staleness verdict stated — stale evidence freezes AS
  stale, loudly, never laundered fresh;
- `requirements.md` — the requirements set as of the freeze: statuses, the
  WP.22 approval stamps, open questions, change-request dispositions;
- `frames/` — Figma exports for every requirement that pins a frame (skipped
  with a stated note when FIGMA_ACCESS_TOKEN or the API is absent);
- `RECORD.md` — the manifest, including a signature-references section: each
  externally signed work product (agreement / uat / acceptance) is either a
  human-entered pointer (`ultra records sign <wp> --ref <pointer>`) or an
  explicit UNSIGNED marker.

A version freezes ONCE; re-freezing refuses without `--force`, because
evidence rewriting must be loud. The frozen directory commits WITH the
release, by a human — the freeze never commits.

**There are deliberately no empty record templates in this directory.**
Records are created BY the acts, not filled into forms: `ultra req approve`
writes the WP.22 validation stamp into the requirement file at the moment
the human approves; a customer signature exists only in the customer's
world and is pointed at, never fabricated. A blank template would invite an
agent to complete a record no act produced — the exact failure mode this
harness exists to make impossible.
